cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "trueppm-scheduler: A pure-Python critical-path and Monte Carlo schedule-risk engine"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-light, Apache-2.0 Python library for project scheduling. Computes
  a full critical-path method (CPM) schedule with all four dependency types,
  dependency lag counted in calendar days (the resulting date is
  snapped to the successor's next working day), total and free float, and cycle detection, and forecasts
  delivery risk with PERT-Beta Monte Carlo simulation producing P50/P80/P95
  completion dates.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kelly
    family-names: Hair
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://gitlab.com/trueppm/trueppm/-/tree/main/packages/scheduler"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/trueppm-scheduler/"
keywords:
  - scheduling
  - critical-path
  - cpm
  - monte-carlo
  - pert
  - project-management
  - schedule-risk
  - risk-analysis
